SOAPBOX: Past weekend we had a great time again with the OT7T Team
SOAPBOX: dsitributed more or less over our country . Not as many operators
SOAPBOX: as we had hoped but nevertheless a good result . Bands where
SOAPBOX: distributed to several locations as there where :
SOAPBOX: 10 m at ON6VL - Vito alone
SOAPBOX: 15 m at ON4AMX - ( Clubstation of HCC OR6T ) Ops ON4AMX and ON4ALY Marc and Xavier
SOAPBOX: 20 m at ON7TK-Ops:ON5OO,ON5RA,OR2F,and heavy tech man ON4CJK,Jacques ,
SOAPBOX: Pascal,Ljubo and Jose with their hosts Carine ON7LX and Claude ON7TK
SOAPBOX: 40 m at OR7K - Joseph OR7K,Fero ON9EEE and Jelle ON6PJ
SOAPBOX: 80 m at ON7TK - Ops ON5OO,ON5RA,OR2F
SOAPBOX: 160 m at ON4DS and ON4AMX - Jim and Marc
SOAPBOX: Multiplier chasers where Pat ON4AMI,Thierry ON4TH,Jim ON4DS
SOAPBOX: Switching bands and locations was very often
SOAPBOX: necessary for multiple reasons such as minibreak for eating ,
SOAPBOX: bathroomvisits , but not for tech problems at all .We had nil
SOAPBOX: problems with the network or with logging into N1MMplus.Only
SOAPBOX: little issue was the few Ops left to finish of the contest as
SOAPBOX: most of the others had to get home and work on monday. We will
SOAPBOX: have to get some more retirees into the team .Condx where
SOAPBOX: pretty bad especially on saturday with heavy arctic flutter
SOAPBOX: especially on 15 . It was great to be with all of us together
SOAPBOX: even in a distance . The mood was great . Thank You all and
SOAPBOX: especially all the hosts and hostess Carine . Thanks for the
SOAPBOX: qso's , sorry for those we missed . Let us keep silent for a
SOAPBOX: while sometimes for all the 2025 Silent keys and the peoples in
SOAPBOX: distress all over the world . Till the next big ones .
SOAPBOX: Best dx and 73 / 88
SOAPBOX: Jim ON4DS / OP5T Team leader
